flowchart TB
  accTitle: Which task an event of an issue gives the AI
  accDescr: An event of a bot, on a pull request, or a new issue that a maintainer opened gives the AI no task. Otherwise, a new issue, or the command /assistant again, gives it triage. An answer of the reporter to the assistant's questions gives it follow-up, at most twice and only while no maintainer joined the conversation since the questions. A comment of a maintainer on a reporter's issue that waits for nobody gives it maintainer-reply. A comment of the reporter within 30 days after a release closed the issue gives it release-reply. A maintainer's command /assistant ask gives it maintainer-question. Any other event, such as a comment of someone else, gives it no task. On an issue with the label assistant-muted, only a command of a maintainer starts a task. A task runs only while the AI is on and its secret is set; otherwise no analysis comes, and labels, reminders and closing go on.
  start(["an event of an issue"]) --> who{"a bot, a pull<br>request, or a<br>maintainer's<br>new issue?"}
  who -- "yes" --> none["no task"]
  who -- "no" --> what{"what<br>happened?"}
  what --> triage["`**triage**<br>a new issue,<br>or /assistant<br>again`"]
  what --> followup["`**follow-up**<br>the reporter<br>answered; at most<br>twice, and no<br>maintainer since`"]
  what --> reply["`**maintainer-reply**<br>a maintainer<br>wrote on a<br>reporter's issue<br>that waits<br>for nobody`"]
  what --> persists["`**release-reply**<br>the reporter<br>wrote within<br>30 days after<br>a release<br>closed it`"]
  what --> question["`**maintainer-question**<br>a maintainer<br>asked with<br>/assistant ask`"]
  what -- "anything else" --> none
  triage & followup & reply & persists & question --> muted{"muted, and<br>no command of<br>a maintainer?"}
  muted -- "yes" --> none
  muted -- "no" --> on{"the AI on,<br>and its<br>secret set?"}
  on -- "yes" --> analyze["`**analyze**<br>the AI reads<br>and answers`"]
  on -- "no" --> paused["no analysis;<br>labels, reminders<br>and closing go on"]
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef question fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef ai fill:#8250df33,stroke:#8250df,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  class start trigger
  class who,what,muted,on question
  class triage,followup,reply,persists,question,analyze ai
  class none,paused job
